<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tahoua</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tahoua is a town in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a>, capital of the Tahoua Region. It lies in the Ader, on the frontier between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hausa">Hausa</a> farming lands and the pastures of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuareg">Tuareg</a> confederations such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iwellemmeden">Iwellemmeden</a> Kel Dinnik and the Kel Gres. It is a market for livestock and grain.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tahoua.jpg" alt="Tahoua" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Barke11 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gare_routi%C3%A8re_de_Tahoua_04.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
